faster-whisper>=1.0.0
# Speaker-embedding voice verification (services/voice_auth.py). Not listed
# here, but resemblyzer has a hard `torch` dependency — see Dockerfile's
# own comment for why that's installed from PyTorch's CPU-only wheel index
# BEFORE this file, rather than letting it resolve from the default index
# (which serves the much larger CUDA-bundled build this CPU-only,
# GPU-less container would otherwise silently end up with). CI (test.yml,
# via requirements.lock.txt) doesn't do that CPU-index-first trick — it
# never has — so the lockfile below hash-pins the SAME default-index
# (CUDA-bundled) torch build CI's own fresh installs have always resolved
# transitively; this closes the reproducibility gap without changing what
# CI actually installs. PyTorch's CPU-only index is unreachable from the
# sandbox that authored this lockfile (confirmed: a direct request to
# download.pytorch.org gets a 403 from the egress proxy — see this
# repo's own note on the same limitation in Dockerfile), so generating a
# CPU-pinned lockfile entry would need to happen from an environment that
# can actually reach that index; tracked as a possible follow-up, not
# done here.
