# Not used directly — pinned explicitly because torch/ctranslate2 declare it
# as a runtime dependency, which pip-compile's hash-checking mode (--generate-
# hashes) requires be resolvable and hashed like any other package. Capped
# below 81: setuptools removed the bundled `pkg_resources` module starting
# around that release, and webrtcvad (a resemblyzer transitive dependency,
# imported by services/voice_auth.py) still does `import pkg_resources` the
# old way — an unconstrained pin here resolves to the newest setuptools and
# breaks voice authentication at import time. Verified directly: 75.8.0
# still ships pkg_resources (deprecated but present); pip's own default
# venv bootstrap setuptools happened to mask this before hash-locking
# existed, since nothing previously forced setuptools to a specific version.
setuptools<84
